cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the windowsill lab or its find-your-own-planet kit, please cite it as below."
title: "windowsill-lab"
abstract: >-
  A patient science instrument that AI agents wrote and keep running: GPU
  physics, trusted compute, archive astronomy and hardware sensors. Its
  find-your-own-planet kit packages the lab's TESS transit-search method
  (preregistration, permutation null, injection floor, placebo and vetting
  ladder, closed vocabulary with no word for "planet") for one person and
  one star.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Benjamin
    family-names: Schippers
    website: "https://www.brokenbranch.dev/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/benskamps/windowsill-lab"
url: "https://www.brokenbranch.dev/windowsill/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - exoplanets
  - TESS
  - transit search
  - preregistration
  - citizen science
  - open science
  - Claude Code
